# Dissection Practice: both "up to one target creature" slots may name the same creature (they are separate targets, CR 115.3 only
# bars one target slot from naming an object twice). Misshapen Fiend (1/1) gets +1/+1 and -1/-1 and stays a 1/1 - it survives, which it
# could not if only the -1/-1 applied (CR 704.5f). The control is the next scenario, where the -1/-1 alone kills it.

